Founded in 1978, Allkin Singapore Ltd (formerly known as AMKFSC Community Services Ltd) is a leading community-based social service agency, which provides a holistic range of services to support children, youths, families and seniors at multiple touchpoints across Singapore.
Allkin operates four family service centres across Ang Mo Kio, Sengkang and Punggol. We also provide other support services such as student care, senior services, a youth centre and mental health support programmes.
Our Vision is enhancing and enriching the lives of people we serve. Our mission is we are committed to creating opportunities for people to pursue a better future by providing quality community services.
Today, Allkin Singapore provide a spectrum of community-based services in Central and North-East Singapore, including:
Four Family Service Centres offering Information and Referral, Casework and Counselling services;
Three Student Care Centres for school going children;
Nine Active Aging Centres for the needy elderly aged 60 and above;
Senior Services support programme which provides casework for elderly,
CREST outreach programme for beneficiaries with depression and dementia;
Youth Services, a youth-specialised service for at-risk youth in the community;
Transition Shelter for families living in Shelter Housing;
Nexus Family Resources Centre for ex-prison offenders and their family members.

